[1m[38;5;231mWhat redaction posture should the logger enforce?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mKey-pattern + no-credentials rule (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mRecursive key-name redaction (password/token/secret/auth) as a backstop, plus a design rule that credential objects
[39m     [38;5;246mare never passed in — log presence, not values. Pragmatic; fails open on unanticipated key names.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Allowlist only
     [38;5;246mOnly explicitly-declared fields are serialized, everything else dropped. Fails closed, which is the safer direction
[39m     [38;5;246mfor an auth flow. Adds friction at every log site.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both: allowlist for browser, patterns for Node
     [38;5;246mStrict allowlist on the sink that could ship off-device, looser key-pattern redaction for local Node stdout. More [39m
     [38;5;246mcode, but matches risk to destination.[39m
